{
  "about": "The waiting-fields program, fix 1 (2026-11-24, lane A2). How the Identified by IRN reads when no label carries it and no approved source looks it up. The server's counts (application/review_summary.review_summary and no_source_fields, tests/test_field_review_words.py) and the app's field rows (field_presentation.fieldReviewStatus, test/field_review_words_contract_test.dart) both read this file. `no_approved_authority` is the server's field_research.contracts.NO_APPROVED_AUTHORITY: such a field that research left unknown with no value, and that no reason names, is not counted for review and reads 'Not on labels' (`no_source`). An unknown one with text in a value layer, or with a reason naming it, needs review as before; in any other state it follows the ordinary rule (an unresolved one needs review, a supported value or a settled absence does not). The app also keeps an unknown one holding an authority match for review, which the server's projected fields cannot show. Each case: the fields (state, has_value), the reason codes, the disposition, the server's summary (the queue row's counts) and each field row's word (review, no_source, settled, or none for a settled absence).",
